Article 8
(1) Prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women is carried out in the following fields:

a. education;
b. health;
c. religion;
d. security;
e. justice;
f. public works and spatial planning;
g. public housing and residential areas;
h. social affairs;
i. labor;
j. women's empowerment and child protection;
k. defense;
l. environment;
m. population administration and civil registration;
n. population control and family planning;
o. transportation;
p. communication and informatics;
q. cooperatives, small and medium enterprises;
r. youth and sports;
s. culture;
t. tourism;
u. trade and industry; and
v. other fields.

(2) Prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by:

a. developing communication media, information, education and public campaigns through media;
b. developing educational materials and curriculum in accordance with regional authority;
c. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
d. building early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, boarding educational environments, and other public spaces;
e. implementing consultation services for families, prospective brides and grooms, students, Islamic students, youth, university students and vulnerable groups;
f. encouraging behavioral change of parents and society;
g. developing regional policies, schools, boarding schools, and universities that are safe and friendly for women and integrated with regional spatial planning policies;
h. establishing and developing cadres, communities, young people, students, Islamic students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, community leaders and religious leaders for prevention;
i. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media;
j. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable women groups;
k. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
l. increasing the capacity of City Regional Government, government agencies, educational institutions, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, business sector, service institutions, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities;
m. conducting cooperation with religious institutions, community social institutions, service institutions, universities, media, youth organizations, religious leaders and community leaders; and
n. conducting socialization of laws and regulations.

(3) The fields and forms of prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are implemented by agencies, regional apparatus, institutions, community institutions, organizations, communities, professional institutions that handle related affairs in accordance with their authority based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 3
The Protection of Women aims to:
a. prevent all forms of violence, exploitation, and discrimination against women;
b. provide services and recovery for women victims of violence, exploitation and discrimination;
c. realize the capacity of the City Regional Government in implementing the Protection of Women from violence, exploitation and discrimination;
d. increase community participation in the Protection of Women; and
e. realize a social life that is safe and free from all forms of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women.

Article 4
The scope of regulation for the implementation of Women's Protection includes:
a. women's rights;
b. prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women;
c. services;
d. coordination and cooperation;
e. community participation;
f. data and information systems;
g. institutional matters;
h. obligations of the City Regional Government;
i. control, guidance and supervision;
j. awards; and
k. financing.

Article 7
Prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women is intended to create a safe environment for women and to reduce vulnerability to violence, exploitation and discrimination against vulnerable groups of women, as follows:
a. women in disaster and social conflict situations; b. women with disabilities; c. women with HIV/AIDS;
d. women migrant workers;
e. girls;
f. women heads of household;
g. women domestic workers;
h. home-based women workers;
i. elderly women;
j. informal women workers;
k. women in situations of intolerance; and
l. other vulnerable groups of women.

Article 2
The Protection of Women is based on:
a. respect for human dignity;
b. non-discrimination;
c. the best interests of the victim;
d. justice;
e. benefit; and
f. legal certainty.
